    "bookends": {
      "first": {
        "speaker": 0,
        "line": 1,
        "text": "As a girl, you see the world like a giant candy store, filled with sweet candy and such. But one day you look around and see a prison and you're on death row. You wanna run, or scream or cry. But something's locking you up."
      },
      "last": {
        "speaker": 0,
        "line": 580,
        "text": "That day I read the story Holden wrote for me. It was kinda different from the other one, but kinda the same. It was about a woman who was put upon. Whose job was a prison, and whose life had lost all meaning. Other people don't get her, especially her husband."
      }
